WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.861
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:06.161 --> 00:00:09.350
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:17.051
Unit twenty: A Trip to the Countryside. In this unit, you will describe the countryside and village life.

4
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.179
Countryside.

5
00:00:19.879 --> 00:00:23.690
Countryside means land outside the city with farms and fields.

6
00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:26.453
My grandparents live in the countryside.

7
00:00:27.153 --> 00:00:29.736
Your turn. Say: Countryside.

8
00:00:32.436 --> 00:00:33.484
Countryside.

9
00:00:34.483 --> 00:00:35.322
Village.

10
00:00:36.022 --> 00:00:38.962
Village means a very small town in the countryside.

11
00:00:39.262 --> 00:00:41.157
Their village is near a river.

12
00:00:41.857 --> 00:00:45.020
Your turn. Say: Village.

13
00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:48.454
Village.

14
00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:50.544
Rice field.

15
00:00:51.244 --> 00:00:54.706
Rice field means a wet field where rice grows.

16
00:00:55.006 --> 00:00:56.739
The rice fields are green.

17
00:00:57.439 --> 00:00:59.964
Your turn. Say: Rice field.

18
00:01:02.664 --> 00:01:03.734
Rice field.

19
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:05.426
Cow.

20
00:01:06.126 --> 00:01:09.078
Cow means a big farm animal that gives milk.

21
00:01:09.378 --> 00:01:10.890
I help feed the cow.

22
00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:14.207
Your turn. Say: Cow.

23
00:01:16.907 --> 00:01:17.734
Cow.

24
00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:19.728
Palm tree.

25
00:01:20.428 --> 00:01:24.181
Palm tree means a tall tree with big leaves at the top.

26
00:01:24.481 --> 00:01:26.735
There are many palm trees in Cambodia.

27
00:01:27.435 --> 00:01:30.459
Your turn. Say: Palm tree.

28
00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.149
Palm tree.

29
00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:35.930
Quiet.

30
00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.746
Quiet means with very little noise.

31
00:01:39.046 --> 00:01:41.185
The village is quiet at night.

32
00:01:41.885 --> 00:01:44.050
Your turn. Say: Quiet.

33
00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:47.600
Quiet.

34
00:01:48.583 --> 00:01:49.526
Fresh air.

35
00:01:50.226 --> 00:01:53.062
Fresh air means clean, cool air.

36
00:01:53.362 --> 00:01:54.885
I love the fresh air.

37
00:01:55.585 --> 00:01:58.191
Your turn. Say: Fresh air.

38
00:02:00.891 --> 00:02:01.823
Fresh air.

39
00:02:02.817 --> 00:02:04.131
Grandparents.

40
00:02:04.831 --> 00:02:07.934
Grandparents means the parents of your mother or father.

41
00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:10.709
I visit my grandparents in the holidays.

42
00:02:11.409 --> 00:02:15.420
Your turn. Say: Grandparents.

43
00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.237
Grandparents.

44
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.714
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:23.014 --> 00:02:25.698
Rithy, where did you go in the holidays?

46
00:02:26.983 --> 00:02:29.563
I visited my grandparents in the countryside.

47
00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.362
What is their village like?

48
00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:37.951
It's quiet. There is a big rice field, and there are many palm trees.

49
00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.634
Is there a big shop?

50
00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:45.659
No, there isn't. But there is fresh air and a friendly cow!

51
00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:50.378
Grammar focus: There is and There isn't.

52
00:02:50.678 --> 00:02:54.143
There is a rice field. There isn't a big shop.

53
00:02:54.443 --> 00:02:59.742
'There isn't' means 'there is not'. Use 'a' or 'an' after it: There isn't a cinema.

54
00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:04.076
Now read and listen. Holidays in the Village.

55
00:03:04.376 --> 00:03:07.989
In the holidays, I visit my grandparents in the countryside.

56
00:03:09.283 --> 00:03:13.825
Their village is quiet, with tall palm trees and green rice fields.

57
00:03:15.117 --> 00:03:18.150
There isn't a big shop, but there is a small market.

58
00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.274
Every morning, I help Grandpa feed the cow.

59
00:03:23.583 --> 00:03:26.941
I love the fresh air and listening to Grandma's stories.

60
00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:30.844
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.527
There blank a big shop in the village.

62
00:03:33.827 --> 00:03:37.596
A, isn't. B, aren't. C, not.

63
00:03:41.583 --> 00:03:43.606
The answer is A: isn't.

64
00:03:45.117 --> 00:03:47.697
A wet field where rice grows is a blank.

65
00:03:47.997 --> 00:03:53.368
A, rice field. B, palm tree. C, village.

66
00:03:57.383 --> 00:04:00.079
The answer is A: rice field.

67
00:04:01.583 --> 00:04:03.699
The parents of your mother are your blank.

68
00:04:03.999 --> 00:04:09.173
A, grandparents. B, cousins. C, neighbours.

69
00:04:13.183 --> 00:04:15.554
The answer is A: grandparents.

70
00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:22.222
Now it's your turn to speak. What is different between the city and the countryside?

71
00:04:27.522 --> 00:04:34.911
In the city, there is a lot of traffic. In the countryside, there isn't much traffic, and there is fresh air.

72
00:04:35.211 --> 00:04:36.943
Excellent answer, Rithy!

73
00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:42.413
Great work today! You learned eight new words and there is and there isn't.

74
00:04:42.713 --> 00:04:47.490
Today's value is respect for elders. Listen to and help older people.

75
00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:50.907
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

76
00:04:51.207 --> 00:04:53.848
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

